WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.140
It's a good thing Charlie Hunnam didn't play
Christian Grey.

00:00:03.360 --> 00:00:08.040
Turns out, there's one thing the Sons of Anarchy
alum and Triple Frontier star can't stand

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:12.420
to do as part of his job, and it's the one
thing many others might enjoy the most: Charlie

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.320
Hunnam hates filming love scenes.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:20.380
In a 2017 interview with Elle, Hunnam explained
that making out with women on camera isn't

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:25.640
only a lot less glamorous than it appears
to be, but it's also kind of terrifying, due

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:28.430
in part to the fact that he's huge germophobe.

00:00:28.430 --> 00:00:29.940
The actor told the publication,

00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:33.380
"I've been profoundly germophobic since I
was a young child."

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.540
Hunnam shared with Elle that his germophobia
began when he was only eight or nine years

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:40.900
old, after having learned about a parasite
that caused blindness.

00:00:41.280 --> 00:00:42.080
He explained,

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.800
"There was a parasite from dogs in the north
of England that, if you ingested it, could

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.560
turn you blind.

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:52.030
We had a thing in schools to educate the kids
about the importance of hygiene, specifically

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:55.160
around dogs, because we had a few kids who
went blind.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.740
That horrified me."

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:01.020
As an adult, the actor has had a difficult
time getting intimate on screen.

00:01:01.020 --> 00:01:03.380
"You'd think that would be the best part of
the job, right?"

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:03.880
"Yeah."

00:01:03.880 --> 00:01:04.380
"No.

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.420
I wake up in cold sweats that day."

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:10.660
But Hunnam's germophobia is only part of the
reason why he hates shooting love scenes.

00:01:10.920 --> 00:01:15.980
He's also keenly aware of the effect his job
as a leading man has on his jewelry designer

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.360
girlfriend, Morgana McNelis.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:18.480
He told Elle,

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:23.220
"I'm in a very committed relationship, and
I'm also cognizant that it's not my girlfriend's

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:24.540
favorite part of my job."

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:29.130
So when Hunnam is forced to feign intimacy,
he does so knowing that there's a fine line

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.240
he'll have to walk.

00:01:30.520 --> 00:01:35.030
Part of being an actor is making a scene believable,
which means that he has to make a real connection

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:36.660
with the person that he's working with.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:41.760
But, as he explained to Elle, it's also important
that it's clear that any on-set intimacy is

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:45.220
entirely fabricated — and won't spill over
into the real world.

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:46.320
Hunnam said,

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:50.520
"I try to be sensitive to the fact that we're
doing something intimate, but also keep a

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:55.070
clear boundary […] It's a delicate balance
to strike - to be emotionally open enough

00:01:55.070 --> 00:02:00.110
to have an experience that feels honest between
two people but also maintain that it's just

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:00.860
for the film.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.440
It's not my favorite thing to do.

00:02:02.680 --> 00:02:05.520
I don't want to kiss anyone but my girlfriend
for my whole life."

00:02:05.900 --> 00:02:10.799
Fortunately, Hunnam has never felt objectified
by others in the industry, and has evidently

00:02:10.799 --> 00:02:14.470
had an easy enough time getting people to
respect his feelings and understand where

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:16.540
he's coming from regarding love scenes.

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:20.800
When asked if he felt more like an object
to ogle than a living, breathing person, he

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:21.300
said,

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.720
"I don't view myself that way.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:27.120
I obviously am cognizant of the fact that
being handsome gives me greater breadth of

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:27.960
opportunity.

00:02:28.129 --> 00:02:32.440
I'd hope that what I bring to the table far
surpasses just being handsome."

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.510
So, all things considered, it's probably for
the best that the actor wound up dropping

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:39.780
out of the first 50 Shades of Grey film back
in 2015.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:44.000
Hunnam had cited scheduling conflicts as the
reason for his departure - he had already

00:02:44.010 --> 00:02:48.680
promised to be in Crimson Peak - but perhaps
coming to terms with the full extent of 50

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:53.079
Shades of Grey's romantic content had something
to do with pushing him in that direction.

00:02:53.079 --> 00:02:57.659
Either way, Hunnam maintains that having to
let go of playing Grey was a huge disappointment

00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:02.160
for him, especially since he had bonded with
the film's director, Sam Taylor-Johnson.

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:03.080
He told Elle,

00:03:03.440 --> 00:03:05.780
"That was a somewhat traumatic experience
for me.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.200
I didn't want to open that wound."

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:12.100
Call it germophobia, or call it true love
and an undying commitment to his girlfriend.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:16.680
Whatever the reasoning, Charlie Hunnam will
likely never be an actor who loves stripping

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:18.080
down with his co-stars.

00:03:18.240 --> 00:03:19.240
As he explained,

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.370
"The point is, everyone thinks it's great
to be an actor and get to kiss a bunch of

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.900
beautiful actresses in films, but I actually
hate it."

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:29.319
"I wouldn't even use my girlfriend's toothbrush.

00:03:29.319 --> 00:03:30.860
That's just disgusting."

